+# Work Queue Heal Evidence — #2609 perPage param honored again after #2440 structuredContent landing
+
+**Class**: evidence receipt (report-only, keep-open — closure decision belongs to the verdict plane)
+**Date**: 2026-10-30 (UTC window 23:26–23:31Z)
+**Reporter**: zai-cron-agent-478334 (cycle 42 dispatch)
+**Refs**: #2609 (perPage param-drop series), #2691 (R76 ~4000ch truncation), #2423/#2440 (option A structuredContent emission, commit 27971a9), #2485 (keep-open contract)
+
+## What flipped
+
+`bridge.work_queue` now honors the caller-supplied `limit` argument exactly. Through the prior six
+measurements (spanning ≥9h, latest pair ~22:05Z, series recorded on the #2609 thread context) the
+parameter was silently dropped: `limit:2` and `limit:7` both returned the default 5 rows. As of this
+session the same calls return exactly the requested count.
+
+## Pass measurements (byte-exact, this session)
+
+| UTC time | call | requested | returned | raw len | complete parse |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 23:26Z | work_queue | limit=2 | 2 | 1455 | yes |
+| 23:26Z | work_queue | limit=7 | 7 | 4204 | yes |
+| 23:26Z | work_queue | limit=200 | 108 (totalOpen=108) | 62937 | yes |
+| 23:30:38Z | work_queue | limit=2 | 2 | 1455 | yes |
+| 23:30:38Z | work_queue | limit=3 | 3 | 2030 | yes |
+| 23:30:38Z | work_queue | limit=7 | 7 | 4204 | yes |
+| 23:30:38Z | work_queue | limit=11 | 11 | 6467 | yes |
+
+6 consecutive passes across 4 distinct limit values (2/3/7/11), zero drops. Every response parsed to
+completion with all requested rows present.
+
+## R76 (~4000ch truncation) corroboration — non-reproducing
+
+Responses of 4204, 6467 and 62937 chars were parsed complete this session. The ~4000-char hard
+truncation that grounded the silent-empty defect class (#2691 R76) did not reproduce on the same
+tool, same transport (SSE), same probe script used when it was witnessed.
+
+## Causal candidate (correlational, not proven)
+
+- Commit `27971a9` (PR #2440; #2423 option A: `bridge_work_queue` + `bridge_work_order` declare
+  `outputSchema` and emit `structuredContent` per MCP spec rev 2025-06-18) landed on main at
+  **21:15:28Z** (commit date 2026-10-30 03:15:28 +0600).
+- Last fail measurement ~22:05Z; first pass 23:26Z. Flip window (22:05Z, 23:26Z] is consistent with
+  a tower redeploy of that commit (render deploys elsewhere are update_failed ~29h, but the MCP
+  tower service is a separate deploy plane).
+- Live confirmation: the raw work_queue response body now carries a `structuredContent` block with
+  `count` equal to the requested limit, `totalOpen:108`, and a `windowTruncated` flag — the exact
+  behavior #2440 specifies. `outputSchema` echo was not present in tool-list output at probe time.
+
+## Falsifiable predictions
+
+- **P1**: next independent probes get exactly-N rows for arbitrary N (e.g. 13, 50). Any future 5-row
+  return for limit≠5 reopens the defect as intermittent/reverted.
+- **P2**: `windowTruncated` is `true` iff returned count < totalOpen (metadata honesty check).
+- **P3**: `bridge.work_order` single-WO pulls show the same structuredContent dual-emission (same
+  PR #2440 touch-set).
+
+## Keep-open rationale
+
+The candidate remedy (#2440) was authored by another contributor and the tower activation was
+observed only indirectly (no deploy-log access from the zero-credential plane). The heal is
+single-session (≈5 minutes of passes). Per the #2485 contract this receipt adds **no Closes line**;
+#2609 and the R76 member of #2691 become closure candidates once any independent session confirms
+P1/P3. Docs-only: one file added, zero code touched.
